init: starting sh
$ lazytest
==== Q4: lazytest (LAZY heap allocation) ====

-- T1: sbrk(32 MB) must not allocate memory --
[before sbrk]
   free_pages=56788  user_pages(sz)=4  resident=4  user_pt=1
[after sbrk(32MB), nothing touched]
   free_pages=56788  user_pages(sz)=8196  resident=4  user_pt=1
   PASS: free_pages unchanged by sbrk(32MB)
   PASS: sz grew by 8192 pages
   PASS: no new resident pages

-- T2: touch 5 widely spaced pages --
[after touching 5 pages]
   free_pages=56779  user_pages(sz)=8196  resident=9  user_pt=5
   PASS: exactly 5 pages became resident
   PASS: free_pages dropped by 5 data pages + the new page-table pages
   (page-table pages added: 4, because the pages lie in different 4 MB regions)
   PASS: values written to the lazily mapped pages read back correctly

-- T3: untouched page reads as zero --
[after READING one untouched page]
   free_pages=56777  user_pages(sz)=8196  resident=10  user_pt=6
   PASS: byte read from untouched page is 0
   PASS: the read faulted in exactly one frame

-- T4: fork / exit with a sparse heap --
[parent just before fork]
   free_pages=56777  user_pages(sz)=8196  resident=10  user_pt=6
   child: inherited data in touched pages: OK
[child, after fork and one private write]
   free_pages=56694  user_pages(sz)=8196  resident=11  user_pt=6
[parent while child is alive]
   free_pages=56694  user_pages(sz)=8196  resident=10  user_pt=6
   fork consumed 83 frames (only touched pages were copied, not 8192)
   PASS: fork of a 32MB lazy heap is cheap (<300 frames)
[parent after child exited and was reaped]
   free_pages=56777  user_pages(sz)=8196  resident=10  user_pt=6
   PASS: free_pages back to the value before fork (no leak)
   PASS: parent's page unaffected by child's write (isolation)
[parent after that read (1 more page faulted in)]
   free_pages=56776  user_pages(sz)=8196  resident=11  user_pt=6

-- T5: system calls on untouched user buffers --
[before syscalls]
   free_pages=56776  user_pages(sz)=8196  resident=11  user_pt=6
   PASS: write(pipe) from untouched buffer returned 64
   PASS: read(pipe) into untouched buffer returned 64
   PASS: read(file) into untouched buffer got README text
   first bytes: NOTE: we have stopped maintaining the x8...
   PASS: getmeminfo() filled a struct living in an untouched page
[after syscalls]
   free_pages=56771  user_pages(sz)=8196  resident=15  user_pt=7
   resident pages added by the kernel on our behalf: 4

-- T6: invalid accesses must kill only the offender --
   child A: writing at address >= sz (0x2006000)
pid 5 lazytest: segfault at 0x2006000 eip 0x549: address >= sz (beyond heap) -- kill proc
   child B: writing into the stack guard page (0x2000)
pid 6 lazytest: segfault at 0x2000 eip 0x508: protection violation (e.g. stack guard page) -- kill proc
   child C: reading kernel address 0x80000000
pid 7 lazytest: segfault at 0x80000000 eip 0x6b0: kernel address -- kill proc
   parent still running after three killed children
   PASS: kernel and parent survived all invalid accesses

-- T7: shrinking gives back only frames that were allocated --
[before sbrk(-32MB)]
   free_pages=56771  user_pages(sz)=8196  resident=15  user_pt=7
[after sbrk(-32MB)]
   free_pages=56782  user_pages(sz)=4  resident=4  user_pt=7
   frames returned: 11 (= resident pages dropped: 11); page-table pages stay until exit (user_pt=7)
   PASS: every freed frame was a really-allocated page
   PASS: sz is back to the pre-heap size
   PASS: sbrk() refuses to shrink into the stack/guard page
   child D: touching freed heap page after shrink (0xA04000)
pid 8 lazytest: segfault at 0xa04000 eip 0x688: address >= sz (beyond heap) -- kill proc

-- T8: out of physical memory during lazy allocation --
[before OOM test]
   free_pages=56782  user_pages(sz)=4  resident=4  user_pt=7
   child: sbrk(400MB) returned OK; now touching every page...
   child: touched 64 MB
   child: touched 128 MB
   child: touched 192 MB
pid 9 lazytest: lazy alloc out of memory at 0xdd54000 -- kill proc
[after OOM child was killed and reaped]
   free_pages=56782  user_pages(sz)=4  resident=4  user_pt=7
   PASS: all frames returned after the OOM-killed child was reaped

==== lazytest summary: 20 passed, 0 failed ====
